.TH DOUBLETAKE-TEST-RECEIVER 1 "August 2026" "doubletake" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
doubletake-test-receiver \- diagnostic AirPlay mirroring receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doubletake-test-receiver
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doubletake-test-receiver
is a local AirPlay receiver for testing the real
.B doubletake
sender without an Apple TV or other receiver. It performs pairing, RTSP session
setup, timing, event, video, and audio protocol handling, then drains incoming
media while reporting activity statistics.
.PP
It is a diagnostic sink, not a media player: it does not display video or play
audio. By default it listens only on the IPv4 loopback address.
.SH PROTOCOL COVERAGE AND LIMITATIONS
The modern profile advertises and exercises FairPlay SAP (FPSAP). The Roku
profile deliberately omits FPSAP, matching that hardware protocol personality.
.PP
It parses the outer AirPlay video framing and counts video and audio traffic,
but encrypted video and audio payloads are not authenticated, decrypted, or
decoded. The reported counters demonstrate transport flow rather than decoded
media correctness. This program is a diagnostic sink, not a media player or a
receiver-compatibility substitute.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B roku
Exercise the legacy third-party receiver path, including raw pairing, legacy
session setup, plaintext control when authentication permits it, and NTP timing.
FPSAP is deliberately omitted. This is the default.
.TP
.B modern
Exercise the modern receiver path, including HomeKit-style pairing, encrypted
control and event channels, FPSAP, split media setup, and PTP timeline metadata.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
All authenticated modes use the single value supplied by
.B \-code
or
.BR DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE .
The environment variable takes precedence over the command-line option.
.TP
.B none
Allow transient pairing and do not challenge RTSP requests. A code must not be
supplied. This is the default.
.TP
.B pin
Advertise PIN-required pairing and use the code for SRP pair-setup. A
.B /pair-pin-start
request prints the configured code in the receiver log. RTSP Digest
authentication is disabled.
.TP
.B password
Use the code as the configured SRP pairing password without advertising an
on-screen PIN. RTSP Digest authentication is disabled.
.TP
.B digest
Allow transient pairing, then require RFC 2069 Digest authentication for media
session requests using the configured code.
.TP
.B combined
Use the code as a configured fixed password for pair-setup and subsequent RTSP
Digest authentication. This mode does not advertise or display an on-screen
PIN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-listen \fIADDRESS\fR
TCP listen address for the AirPlay control connection. The default is
.BR 127.0.0.1:7000 .
Port 0 requests an ephemeral port; the actual bound address is printed at
startup.
.TP
.B \-profile \fIPROFILE\fR
Receiver protocol profile: \fBroku\fR or \fBmodern\fR. The default is
.BR roku .
.TP
.B \-auth \fIMODE\fR
Authentication mode: \fBnone\fR, \fBpin\fR, \fBpassword\fR, \fBdigest\fR, or
.BR combined .
The default is \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-code \fICODE\fR
Unified pairing and/or Digest code selected by
.BR \-auth .
Authenticated modes require a non-empty code. Prefer the environment variable
to avoid exposing the value in shell history and
.BR ps (1)
output.
.TP
.B \-name \fINAME\fR
Receiver name advertised by
.BR /info .
An empty value uses the selected profile's default.
.TP
.B \-model \fIMODEL\fR
Receiver model advertised by
.BR /info .
An empty value uses the selected profile's default.
.TP
.B \-device-id \fIIDENTIFIER\fR
Receiver device ID advertised by
.BR /info .
An empty value generates a random locally administered identifier for this
process.
.TP
.B \-debug
Enable verbose receiver protocol logging.
.TP
.B \-stats-interval \fIDURATION\fR
Print periodic protocol and media statistics using a Go duration such as
\fB1s\fR or \fB500ms\fR. Zero disables periodic output. Final statistics are
always printed.
.TP
.B \-h, \-help
Show command-line help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE
Pairing/password/Digest code. When set, including to an empty value, it takes
precedence over
.BR \-code .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the default Roku-profile receiver with a configured pairing password:
.B DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE=testpass doubletake-test-receiver \-profile roku \-auth password
.TP
Connect a synthetic sender using that password:
.B DOUBLETAKE_CODE=testpass doubletake \-target 127.0.0.1 \-port 7000 \-test
.TP
Exercise modern pairing and Digest authentication with one shared fixed
password (no on-screen PIN):
.B DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE=4827 doubletake-test-receiver \-profile modern \-auth combined \-stats-interval 2s
.TP
Run an unauthenticated receiver on an ephemeral port:
.B doubletake-test-receiver \-listen 127.0.0.1:0
.PP
Copy the printed
.I PORT
into the sender invocation:
.IP
.B doubletake \-target 127.0.0.1 \-port PORT \-test
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR doubletake (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Omar Roth.
